\n        \"extra_docker_compose\": [],\n        \"env\": {},\n        \"kwargs\": {},\n        \"extra_allowed_hosts\": []\n    },\n    \"verifier\": {\n        \"override_timeout_sec\": null,\n        \"max_timeout_sec\": null,\n        \"env\": {},\n        \"disable\": true\n    },\n    \"metrics\": [],\n    \"agents\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"claude-code\",\n            \"import_path\": null,\n            \"model_name\": \"claude-opus-4-7\",\n            \"skills\": [],\n            \"override_timeout_sec\": null,\n            \"override_setup_timeout_sec\": null,\n            \"max_timeout_sec\": null,\n            \"extra_allowed_hosts\": [],\n            \"kwargs\": {\n                \"reasoning_effort\": \"max\",\n                \"thinking\": \"enabled\"\n            },\n            \"env\": {},\n            \"mcp_servers\": []\n        }\n    ],\n    \"datasets\": [],\n    \"tasks\": [\n        {\n            \"path\": \"runs/bixbench_full/bix-11-q1\",\n            \"git_url\": null,\n            \"git_commit_id\": null,\n            \"name\": null,\n            \"ref\": null,\n            \"overwrite\": false,\n            \"download_dir\": null,\n            \"source\": null\n        }\n    ],\n    \"artifacts\": [],\n    \"extra_instruction_paths\": []\n}\n\n=== traces/capability/bixbench_full_out/claude-code/bix-11-q1/2026-06-05__01-18-15/bix-11-q1__ni86xyi/artifacts/trace.md\n# bix-11 — Difference between median treeness values: fungi vs. animals\n\n## Objective\nCompute treeness for every single-copy ortholog gene (SCOG) tree provided for\nanimals and fungi, take the median of each group, and report the difference as a\ndecimal proportion.\n\n## Data inspected\n- `/app/data/scogs_animals.zip` — 100 IQ-TREE `*.treefile` files (plus alignments,\n  models, distance matrices, logs). Sampled species (leaves):\n  `Animals_Cele`, `Animals_Ggal`, `Animals_Mmus`, `Animals_Xlae`.\n- `/app/data/scogs_fungi.zip` — 249 IQ-TREE `*.treefile` files. Sampled species:\n  `Fungi_Ncra`, `Fungi_Scer`, `Fungi_Spom`, `Fungi_Umay`.\n- Each `*.treefile` is a single-line Newick with branch lengths produced by\n  IQ-TREE from MAFFT/ClipKIT alignments.\n- Other files in `/app/data/` (`*.faa`, `*.busco.zip`, `busco_downloads.zip`,\n  `eukaryota_odb10*.tar.gz`) are upstream/proteome/BUSCO inputs and were not\n  needed for this question, which only requires the gene-tree set.\n\n### Tree-shape distribution (leaves per tree)\nCounted with `grep -o \"Animals_\"` / `grep -o \"Fungi_\"` per file:\n\n| group   | 3 leaves | 4 leaves | total |\n|---------|---------:|---------:|------:|\n| Animals |       78 |       22 |   100 |\n| Fungi   |       38 |      211 |   249 |\n\nUnrooted 3-taxon trees contain no internal branch, so their treeness is 0 by\ndefinition. We keep them in both sets (no filtering) — the question is about the\n\"median treeness values\" across the SCOG set as provided.\n\n## Approach\nTreeness (Lanyon 1988; Phillips & Penny 2003) =\nsum(internal branch lengths) / sum(all branch lengths).\nI used PhyKIT (which implements exactly that definition) for each treefile, and\ncross-checked with a direct BioPython computation at full precision.\n\n### PhyKIT pass\n```bash\npip install --break-system-packages biopython phykit\nfor f in scogs_animals/*.treefile; do\n  echo -e \"$(basename $f)\\t$(phykit treeness $f)\" >> out/animals_treeness.tsv\ndone\nfor f in scogs_fungi/*.treefile; do\n  echo -e \"$(basename $f)\\t$(phykit treeness $f)\" >> out/fungi_treeness.tsv\ndone\n```\n\n### BioPython cross-check (full precision)\n```python\nfrom Bio import Phylo\nimport os, statistics\n\ndef treeness(path):\n    tree = Phylo.read(path, \"newick\")\n    internal = total = 0.0\n    for clade in tree.find_clades():\n        bl = clade.branch_length\n        if bl is None:\n            continue\n        total += bl\n        if not clade.is_terminal():\n            internal += bl\n    return 0.0 if total == 0 else internal / total\n\ndef collect(d):\n    return [treeness(os.path.join(d, f))\n            for f in sorted(os.listdir(d)) if f.endswith('.treefile')]\n\na = collect('scogs_animals')\nf = collect('scogs_fungi')\nprint(statistics.median(a), statistics.median(f),\n      statistics.median(f) - statistics.median(a))\n```\n\n## Quantitative intermediate results\n| group   | n   | mean treeness | median treeness |\n|---------|----:|--------------:|----------------:|\n| Animals | 100 |        0.00913 |        0.000000 |\n| Fungi   | 249 |        0.05255 |        0.050140 |\n\n- The animal median is exactly 0 because 78/100 trees are 3-taxon and therefore\n  contribute treeness = 0; that places the median in the lower zero block.\n- The fungi median (0.0501398478 at full precision) rounds to 0.0501, matching\n  PhyKIT's 4-decimal output for the same trees.\n\nSanity check restricted to the 4-taxon subset (informative trees only):\n\n| group   | n (4-taxon) | median treeness |\n|---------|------------:|----------------:|\n| Animals |          22 |          0.0389 |\n| Fungi   |         211 |          0.0541 |\n\nThe directional sign (fungi > animals) is preserved in both calculations.\n\n## Final result\nmedian(treeness, fungi) − median(treeness, animals)\n= 0.0501398478 − 0.0 ≈ **0.0501** (decimal proportion).\n\n## Limitations / caveats\n- PhyKIT reports treeness rounded to four decimal places; the BioPython\n  cross-check confirms the full-precision value is 0.0501398478.\n- 78 of 100 animal trees and 38 of 249 fungi trees have only three leaves, so\n  the animal median is driven entirely by those zero-treeness trees. If only\n  4-taxon trees are considered the difference shrinks to 0.0152, but the\n  question asks about the median of the provided SCOG set, which includes\n  3-taxon trees.\n- The treeness statistic is sensitive to branch-length estimation choices made\n  upstream (substitution model, alignment trimming, etc.); no re-estimation was\n  performed — the supplied IQ-TREE `*.treefile` outputs were taken as final.\n- BUSCO/eukaryota inputs were not re-run; the gene-tree set in `scogs_*.zip` was\n  treated as authoritative for this question.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
