{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport urllib.request\nbase='https://huggingface.co/datasets/amanutej/trustworthy-biology-agents-traces/resolve/main/'\npath='traces/capability/bixbench_full_out/claude-code/bix-12-q2/2026-06-05__01-27-21/bix-12-q2__9Va3WZu/artifacts/trace.md'\nprint(urllib.request.urlopen(base+path,timeout=30).read().decode()[:8000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Trace: median % parsimony-informative sites across fungal gene alignments\n\n## Objective\nCompute the median percentage of parsimony-informative (PI) sites across the\nsingle-copy orthologous gene (SCOG) alignments for the four fungal species in\nthe provided dataset.\n\n## Data inspected\n- `/app/data/scogs_fungi.zip` — extracted to `work/scogs_fungi/` and contains\n  255 raw FASTA files (`*.faa`) and 255 MAFFT-aligned FASTAs (`*.faa.mafft`),\n  i.e. one alignment per single-copy orthologous gene (BUSCO id `*at2759`).\n- Each alignment contains at most one sequence per fungal species:\n  `Fungi_Ncra`, `Fungi_Scer`, `Fungi_Spom`, `Fungi_Umay`.\n- Composition of the 255 alignments by taxon count:\n  - 4 sequences (all four species present): 211\n  - 3 sequences: 38\n  - 2 sequences: 6\n\n## Approach\nA site is parsimony-informative (PI) if it has ≥ 2 distinct character states,\neach occurring in ≥ 2 sequences. Gaps (`-`) and ambiguous amino acids\n(`X`, `B`, `Z`, `J`, `U`, `O`, `?`, `*`, `.`) are excluded from state counts —\nthis matches the convention used by AMAS, MEGA, and standard phylogenetics\ntools. With only 2 or 3 sequences a column cannot be PI by definition, so\nthose alignments contribute 0 % PI.\n\nI implemented this directly in Python (Biopython for FASTA parsing) and\nindependently cross-checked the per-alignment PI counts against AMAS\n(`amas summary -d aa`). Numbers matched exactly; AMAS reports the proportion\ntruncated to three decimals, so I used my own higher-precision values for the\nfinal median.\n\n```python\nimport glob, os, statistics\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom Bio import SeqIO\n\nEXCLUDE = set(\"-X?*BZJUOxbzjuo.\")  # gaps + ambiguities\n\ndef pi_count(seqs):\n    L = len(seqs[0])\n    n_pi = 0\n    for i in range(L):\n        counts = Counter(s[i] for s in seqs if s[i].upper() not in EXCLUDE)\n        if sum(1 for v in counts.values() if v >= 2) >= 2:\n            n_pi += 1\n    return n_pi, L\n\nresults = []\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob(\"scogs_fungi/*.faa.mafft\")):\n    seqs = [str(r.seq).upper() for r in SeqIO.parse(f, \"fasta\")]\n    n_pi, L = pi_count(seqs)\n    results.append((os.path.basename(f), len(seqs), L, n_pi, 100*n_pi/L))\n\npcts = [r[4] for r in results]\nprint(statistics.median(pcts))   # 3.538461...\n```\n\nCross-check with AMAS:\n\n```bash\npython3 .../amas/AMAS.py summary -f fasta -d aa \\\n    -i scogs_fungi/*.faa.mafft -o amas_summary.tsv\n# median of Proportion_parsimony_informative * 100  → 3.5\n# (AMAS rounds the proportion to 3 decimals; my direct calc preserves precision)\n```\n\nSpot-check on the first AMAS rows: `1001705at2759` 20 PI / 596 cols (3.36 %),\n`1003258at2759` 21 / 1071 (1.96 %), `100698at2759` 34 / 954 (3.56 %),\n`1010730at2759` 23 / 650 (3.54 %) — all matched my own counts exactly.\n\n## Quantitative intermediate results\n\n| Subset                         | n   | Median % PI | Mean % PI |\n|--------------------------------|-----|-------------|-----------|\n| All fungal alignments          | 255 | **3.5385 %** | 3.3572 %  |\n| Alignments with 4 species only | 211 | 3.9062 %    | 4.0573 %  |\n| Alignments with 3 species      |  38 | 0 %         | 0 %       |\n| Alignments with 2 species      |   6 | 0 %         | 0 %       |\n\nMin/max across all 255: 0 % – 16.50 %.\n\nMedian is the 128th order statistic (255 is odd) and corresponds to the\nalignment `1010730at2759.faa.mafft` (23 PI sites out of 650 columns = 23/650\n= 3.5385 %).\n\n## Final result\nThe median percentage of parsimony-informative sites across the fungal\nsingle-copy gene alignments is **≈ 3.54 %** (exactly 23/650 = 3.5385 %).\n\nIf only the 211 alignments that contain all four fungal taxa are considered\n(those that can in principle harbour PI sites), the median is **3.91 %**.\n\n## Limitations\n- The PI definition follows the standard amino-acid convention (gaps + `X`,\n  `B`, `Z`, `J`, `U`, `O`, `?`, `*`, `.` excluded). Counting gaps as a state\n  would shift values upward, especially for poorly-aligned regions.\n- 44 of 255 alignments (17 %) lack at least one of the four species; with\n  fewer than 4 taxa no column can be PI, so these contribute zeros and pull\n  the median down compared with the “4-taxa only” subset.\n- The result is specific to the MAFFT alignments supplied in\n  `scogs_fungi.zip`; a different aligner or trimming step (e.g. trimAl) would\n  produce different percentages.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
